:MILD_120100 a owl:Class;
  rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000104>;
  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Sibling of treatment plan specification, not a child: a prophylaxis is planned to keep a condition from arising, not to treat one. Named with the plan-specification pattern by decision (2026-09-17); 'method used for prophylaxis' was the alternative."@en;
  rdfs:label "prophylaxis plan specification"@en .

:MILD_120098 a owl:Class;
  rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000033>;
  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A directive information entity that has as part a threshold value and a comparison operator and that is about a quality, such that the quality's meeting the threshold is what the specification prescribes as decisive."@en;
  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Generalises the disease threshold specification (MILD_120029), which is the special case about a phenotypic abnormality. Other specifications with the same shape - a wound healing criterion, an outcome criterion in a trial protocol - are about qualities that are not abnormalities, so they need a parent that does not say 'disease'. Lives in MILD because WONT and any other domain ontology need it and MILD never imports them."@en;
  rdfs:label "threshold specification"@en .

